course: dictionary
lesson: 10374
title: Treasurer: the person who looks after the money
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A treasurer is the person in a club, school council or charity who looks after the money. Context clues help you find this meaning. The phrase «club treasurer» tells you the job belongs to a club.
explain: The sentence says «stealing money that one was trusted to look after, such as a club's treasurer». The clue is "trusted to look after": a treasurer is trusted with the money.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "the person who looks after the money" in place of treasurer. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A treasurer looks after the money, keeps records of what comes in and goes out, and reports on it.
fact: In a school council or club, a pupil may be treasurer, counting money from cake sales.
fact: «Elected treasurer» means the members voted for that person to do the job.
fact: In government, a Treasurer (Australia) or similar official is in charge of the country's money.
fact: Treasurers use maths: they add up the money coming in and subtract the money spent.
exercise: «The club treasurer counted the money from the cake sale.» Who counted the money? | *The treasurer | The caretaker | The chair | The teacher on duty
exercise: What does a treasurer do? | Plays the drums in assembly | *Looks after the money and keeps records of it | Cooks the cakes for the club | Cleans the classroom floor
exercise: «Misappropriation of funds» means stealing money that one was trusted to look after, such as a club's treasurer taking it. What was the treasurer trusted with? | *Looking after the money | Writing the school news | Driving the minibus | Choosing the club's colours
test: Ravi was elected treasurer of the school council. What does "elected" mean here? | Fined for being late | Given a prize for good work | Chosen by the head teacher's dog | *Voted into the job by the members
test: Which job is about looking after the money? | Librarian | Lollipop person | *Treasurer | Goalkeeper
exam: Which sentence uses treasurer correctly? | The treasurer painted the sports hall walls on Monday. | We went to the treasurer for a swim after lunch. | *The club treasurer kept a careful record of every pound we raised. | The treasurer tidied the library shelves into alphabetical order.
